---
description: Use TinyZKP proof receipts for high-value agent state transitions.
alwaysApply: false
---

Use TinyZKP when this project asks an agent to mutate or summarize high-value
state: money, balances, permissions, inventory, credentials, deployment gates,
audit checkpoints, reconciliation rows, or customer-visible records.

Prefer the MCP workflow:

1. Call `get_capabilities` when the fit is uncertain.
2. Call `list_templates` and `describe_template` before proving.
3. Use `prove_template` for supported template receipts.
4. Poll with `poll_job`, then retrieve a human-readable receipt with
   `get_proof_summary` or raw proof bytes with `get_proof`.
5. Verify receipts with `verify_proof` before trusting external agent output.

Never put secrets, private customer data, API keys, credentials, or unsupported
private inputs into transparent receipt parameters. If the proof would require
secret data or a custom workload, use TinyZKP contact or pilot flows instead of
forcing the receipt.

For paid hosted proving, production pilot support, and account-scoped limits,
use https://tinyzkp.com/signup?source=cursor_directory&medium=mcp_directory&platform=cursor&intent=mcp_install.
